Now that you are inside the vps with root, we will create a new user and give it sudo.

The goal is to desable root ssh and only permit connection with user and key, so:

PasswordAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
PermitRootLogin no

1. Create a new user and give it sudo perms
adduser user
(it will ask for a password, remember it)

usermod -aG sudo user

check groups user

2. Copy the authorized_keys file in root/.ssh/ to the new user's ssh folder,
cp /root/.ssh/authorized_keys /home/user/.ssh/authorized_keys

and test if it connects

